conclusion: "At 12 km, a 39.2% longer main battery range (23.65 km to 32.92 km with Spotting Aircraft + Artillery Plotting Room Modification 1) shrinks vertical dispersion from 90.3 m to 75.4 m; horizontal is unchanged at 180 m. With sigma 1.9, half of the shells land within 33.9% of the ellipse (61 m by 30.6 m) and 68.7% within its inner half; a higher sigma packs more shells toward the aim point. Artillery Plotting Room Modification 2 narrows both: horizontal 180 m to 160.2 m, vertical 90.3 m to 80.3 m."
